\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For each fixed $r>=3$, does $C_r$ exist such that for every $n>=r$, every p in (0,1), and every Boolean property of r-uniform hypergraphs invariant under vertex relabeling, $Var_p(f)<=C_r$ $I_p(f)/(\log $ $n)^(r/(r-1))$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For each fixed $r>=3$, does $C_r$ exist such that for every $n>=r$, every p in (0,1), and every Boolean property of r-uniform hypergraphs invariant under vertex relabeling, $Var_p(f)<=C_r$ $I_p(f)/(\log $ $n)^(r/(r-1))$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-uniform-influence-bound-for-hypergraph-properties-October-5-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

